WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.250
In water, lithium fizzes gently.

2
00:00:03.300 --> 00:00:06.470
Potassium bursts into lilac flames.

3
00:00:06.520 --> 00:00:09.870
Yet they sit in the same
group of the periodic table.

4
00:00:09.920 --> 00:00:12.790
Now meet one more element: astatine.

5
00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:17.190
It is so rare and radioactive
that it is very hard to test.

6
00:00:17.240 --> 00:00:19.270
So how can we say how it reacts?

7
00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:20.890
Is it just a guess?

8
00:00:20.940 --> 00:00:25.010
In this mission, you'll meet
three families: the alkali metals,

9
00:00:25.060 --> 00:00:29.030
the halogens, and the noble
gases, which hardly react at all.

10
00:00:29.080 --> 00:00:32.090
You'll find out what makes
each family different.

11
00:00:32.140 --> 00:00:36.740
Your mission: predict how astatine
reacts, without testing it.
